{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-api-v4-medium-mimo-v26pro-rl-max-full200-n02","prediction_set_name":"mimo-v26pro-rl-max-full200-n02","paper_id":"2502.06595","judge_input_sha256":"414b2f1256371a858820fd2ed9aa22e56da9f348e6d143e9a398e8d6dc964214","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2502.06595:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2502.06595:I003:U001","2502.06595:I003:U002","2502.06595:I003:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U001","ISSUE-003:U002","ISSUE-003:U003"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns the missing quantification and invocation range for p in the least-squares estimate. ISSUE-003 instead concerns contradictory domain inclusions and a malformed type for the diffusion matrix in a different theorem; it does not recognize the missing p range.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2502.06595:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-006","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2502.06595:I004:U001","2502.06595:I004:U002","2502.06595:I004:U003","2502.06595:I004:U004","2502.06595:I004:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-006:U001","ISSUE-006:U002","ISSUE-006:U003","ISSUE-006:U004","ISSUE-006:U005"],"same_causal_subject":true,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"Both issues affect the least-squares theorem, but the gold defect is the omission of the extension-amplitude or diffusion-bound factor in an error estimate, demonstrated by scaling. ISSUE-006 instead concerns using the wrong integration measure and an invalid Chebyshev orthogonality step; it does not recognize the missing amplitude dependence. No other prediction supplies that specific scaling defect.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2502.06595:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2502.06595:I005:U001","2502.06595:I005:U002","2502.06595:I005:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U003"],"same_causal_subject":true,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is a quantifier mismatch: the proof supports a fixed-function, function-dependent set and event, not one simultaneous guarantee for the whole class. ISSUE-001 identifies a real/complex optimization-domain mismatch and its effect on the least-squares formula, but does not address the quantifier order, function dependence of S, or uniform event.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}